<item>
            <title>[LU-20898] mdt: file migration does not lock all hard link parents</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20898</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Migrating a regular file with hard links does not reliably lock the parents of its other links before mdd_migrate() rewrites their entries. There are two gaps in mdt_migrate_links_lock():&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. The loop over the linkEA runs while &lt;tt&gt;ldata.ld_lee &amp;amp;&amp;amp; !rc&lt;/tt&gt;. mdt_migrate_link_lock() returns 1 when it takes a LOOKUP lock on a link parent on another MDT, so the loop stops after the first such parent and the remaining link parents are never locked. This dates from &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-4684&quot; title=&quot;DNE3: allow migrating DNE striped directory&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-4684&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-4684&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (commit 169738e30a7e &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-4684&quot; title=&quot;DNE3: allow migrating DNE striped directory&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-4684&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-4684&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; migrate: migrate striped directory&quot;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. The linkEA is read before the source object is locked. A link(), or a cross-directory file rename that does not take the BFL (same MDT since &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17426&quot; title=&quot;parallel cross-directory rename of regular files on single MDT&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-17426&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17426&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and cross-MDT with &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20831&quot; title=&quot;mdt: parallel cross-MDT rename of regular files&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20831&quot;&gt;LU-20831&lt;/a&gt;), can add a link parent in that window. Migration never locks it, but mdd_migrate() rereads the linkEA under the source lock and updates that entry anyway. That parent is changed without its UPDATE lock, and a client&apos;s cached LOOKUP lock on the name can be left pointing at the destroyed source.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both were found while reviewing &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20831&quot; title=&quot;mdt: parallel cross-MDT rename of regular files&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20831&quot;&gt;LU-20831&lt;/a&gt;. Gap 2 was reproduced on a 4-MDT ldiskfs setup only with an injected delay after the linkEA read; neither has been seen in CI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A candidate fix was in patchset 10 of &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69203/10&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69203/10&lt;/a&gt; (lock every link parent; once the source is locked, reread the linkEA and retry from the parent locks if it names an unlocked link parent). It was removed from that change because the issue predates it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
